		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4874&amp;p=35744#p35744"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Yes, I'm using the zumspot 1.3<br><br>On my dm-1701, if i start typing '4000' it is changing the frequency; Where or how do I key up '4000'?  I'm sorry, I'm completely new to this DMR world!!</div></blockquote>Hit # first to enter the TG number. (And read the manual! It's well written and easy to understand.)<br><br>None of this is actually related to OpenGD77 so you'll probably get more help in a general DMR forum. That being said, installing it was the right move, as it's far more intuitive (and powerful!) than the original firmware. At some point, it will all "click" for you and using DMR will become a lot easier. Meanwhile, I'd strongly suggest not setting 91 as static on your hotspot, it's really busy and WILL dominate your reception, just as you've described. Should you want to use it, it can be accessed dynamically with just a few keystrokes.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4063">KC6WOG</a> — Fri Feb 14, 2025 8:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
