		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4874&amp;p=35738#p35738"><![CDATA[
first of all, Please read the manual <a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... r_Guide.md</a><br><br>Secondly, Talk group 91 is very active, hence it is very hard to unlink. I assume your hot spot is a simplex hotspot. If you can hear anything that means your hotspot is transmitting, just like any other simplex transceivers, when it is in transmit it will not hear anything. to be able to key up on tK 4000 to unlink, you need to key in in the gab between the stations, just like if you were to break in. <br><br>another way to unlink is go to brandmeister website, login, then select My device on the left and remove 91 out of static Talk group.<br><br> Hope this help<br>Charlie,<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2843&amp;sid=40cc269ff046060fb3e4a68d59adbee0" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-02-13 at 6.06.32?PM.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Thu Feb 13, 2025 11:08 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
